WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.930
 What's up Marvel fans?

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:02.940
We're here with Jon Favreau,
who plays Happy Hogan.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.890
Now you started
the MCU directing

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.330
Marvel Studios' "Iron Man."

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.400
What is it like to continue
that legacy of Iron Man

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.270
as Happy Hogan?

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.640
 Well, I love being a
part of this as an actor

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.130
because I get to continue
to work with the people

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.770
that I work with on
the "Iron Man" films.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.560
Also, even before I
started directing,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.020
I remember visiting the
set of Spider-Man 3."

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.010
That was my first experience.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.060
So it all feels-- it's nice
that it's all coming together.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.030
And I'm just happy that I've
been able to be a part of it

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.740
in one way or another
for decades now.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:33.540
 That's awesome.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.150
Well, now the entire world
knows who Spider-Man is.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.280
How does that affect Happy?

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.130
 Well, it's-- Happy has
always been in on the secret

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.400
with Tony Stark, with--

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.730
with Peter Parker.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.060
So Happy was always good at
being a professional wingman

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.940
to help out and make-- help
them navigate their way

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.680
through all the challenges of--

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.240
of being a superhero.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.160
I think he offers a
lot of moral support.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.510
I don't think he's--

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.250
I don't think he's too
good for protection,

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.500
even though he's supposed
to be head of security.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.910
But I think he's a good friend.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:06.540
And I think for Peter
Parker, he was a good--

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.980
I think he took it
upon himself to look

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.230
after him after Tony was gone.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.210
So I really like
playing that part.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.980
And I really like
Tom Holland a lot.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:14.850
And I love--

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.910
I love popping onto the
set and working with Jon

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.770
Watts and everybody there.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.450
It's a great group
of young actors.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.190
And as an actor, I love it.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.150
And I think it comes
through in the character.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:25.950
 That's awesome.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.440
Now do you have a favorite
MCU moment in Spider-Man

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.880
through your journey?

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.845
 Oh, in Spider-Man, I like
when we're in the bathroom--

00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:32.370
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.703
I think we're in the
bathroom together--

00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:35.220
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.930
--where I'm trying to
be, like, Nick Fury

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.760
popping into his high school.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.290
And I-- and I confront him.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.160
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.500
And-- and someone
flushes the toilet.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.690
So my really cool,
like, Nick Fury moment

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.870
is completely undermined by--

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.430
by a toilet flushing.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.520
Yeah, I like that one a lot.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.320
 That's awesome.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.700
Jon, thank you so much.
Enjoy the movie.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:54.810
Thank you.
Have a good one.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.860
[MUSIC PLAYING]

